ocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nWhile hiding deprecated configuration properties from extension documentation is arguably a good thing when there is a better replacement (e.g. in case of renaming), it can be confusing, for example when:\n\n* someone finds a property in an old app, and wonders what that property does\n* the property is intended for migration purposes only, and thus is deprecated right from the start, or soon after being introduced (see https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/51006#issuecomment-3540484293)\n\nMaybe we could find a different way to handle deprecated properties, e.g. marking them with a \"deprecated\" tag, or styling them as \"strikethrough\" in the docs?\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nDeprecated configuration properties are documented, though advertised as deprecated.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nDeprecated configuration properties are not documented at all.\n\n### How to Reproduce?\n\n1. Look for `quarkus.transaction-manager.unsafe-multiple-last-resources` in the configuration reference at https://quarkus.io/guides/datasource\n2. Don't find it\n3. Be confused, because it exists: \nhttps://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/2fbc83dc745f870a75560eec67e2bc01a4eb34c6/extensions/narayana-jta/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/narayana/jta/runtime/TransactionManagerBuildTimeConfig.java#L35-L37\n\n### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`\n\n_No response_\n\n### Output of `java -version`\n\n_No response_\n\n### Quarkus version or git rev\n\n_No response_\n\n### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"gsmet","id":1279749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzk3NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1279749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet","html_url":"https://github.com/gsmet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/follow